---
import { Button } from "@/components/ui/button";
import RootLayout from "@/layouts/RootLayout.astro";
import { codeSample } from "../lib/code-sample";
---

<RootLayout>
  <div>
    <div
      class="relative isolate overflow-hidden bg-gradient-to-b from-indigo-100/20"
    >
      <div
        class="mx-auto max-w-7xl pb-24 pt-10 sm:pb-32 lg:grid lg:grid-cols-2 lg:gap-x-8 lg:px-8 lg:py-40"
      >
        <div class="px-6 lg:px-0 lg:pt-4">
          <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl">
            <div class="max-w-lg">
              <h1 class="mt-10">
                Astro +<br />Cloudflare<br />Kickstart Project
              </h1>
              <p class="mt-8 text-subtitle">
                Build and launch with one framework, one vendor, zero hassle.
              </p>
              <div class="mt-10 flex items-center gap-x-6">
                <!--<Button as="a" href="#">Documentation</Button>-->
                <Button as="a" href="/dashboard" variant="default"
                  >Open Taskosaur Dashboard <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></Button
                >
                <Button as="a" href="https://github.com/cooperjones/astro-cloudflare-kickstart" variant="default" target="_blank"
                  >Check it out on GitHub <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></Button
                >
                or
                <Button as="a" href="https://github.com/new?template_name=astro-cloudflare-kickstart" variant="link" target="_blank"
                  >Clone the template repository <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></Button
                >
                
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div
          class="mt-20 sm:mt-24 md:mx-auto md:max-w-2xl lg:mx-0 lg:mt-0 lg:w-screen"
        >
          <div
            class="absolute inset-y-0 right-1/2 -z-10 -mr-10 w-[200%] skew-x-[-30deg] bg-white shadow-xl shadow-indigo-600/10 ring-1 ring-indigo-50 md:-mr-20 lg:-mr-36"
            aria-hidden="true"
          >
          </div>
          <div class="shadow-lg md:rounded-3xl">
            <div
              class="bg-indigo-500 [clip-path:inset(0)] md:[clip-path:inset(0_round_theme(borderRadius.3xl))]"
            >
              <div
                class="absolute -inset-y-px left-1/2 -z-10 ml-10 w-[200%] skew-x-[-30deg] bg-indigo-100 opacity-20 ring-1 ring-inset ring-white md:ml-20 lg:ml-36"
                aria-hidden="true"
              >
              </div>
              <div class="relative px-6 pt-8 sm:pt-16 md:pl-16 md:pr-0">
                <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl md:mx-0 md:max-w-none">
                  <div
                    class="w-screen overflow-hidden rounded-tl-xl bg-gray-900"
                  >
                    <div class="flex bg-gray-800/40 ring-1 ring-white/5">
                      <div
                        class="-mb-px flex text-sm/6 font-medium text-gray-400"
                      >
                        <div
                          class="border-b border-r border-b-white/20 border-r-white/10 bg-white/5 px-4 py-2 text-white"
                        >
                          index.astro
                        </div>
                        <div class="border-r border-gray-600/10 px-4 py-2">
                          astro.config.js
                        </div>
                      </div>
                    </div>
                    <pre
                      class="px-6 pb-14 pt-6 text-white">
                      {codeSample}
                    </pre>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <div
                  class="pointer-events-none absolute inset-0 ring-1 ring-inset ring-black/10 md:rounded-3xl"
                  aria-hidden="true"
                >
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div
        class="absolute inset-x-0 bottom-0 -z-10 h-24 bg-gradient-to-t from-background sm:h-32"
      >
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="page-section page-gap">
      <div class="mx-auto lg:mx-0">
        <p class="text-base/7 font-semibold text-indigo-600">Deploy faster</p>
        <h1 class="mt-2">A Smarter Starting Point for Modern Websites</h1>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-6 text-subtitle">
        In the ever-evolving landscape of web development, getting a project off
        the ground often involves juggling tools, vendors, and architectural
        decisions that can easily spiral into complexity. What if there was a
        way to cut through all of that—an <b>opinionated</b> but <b>flexible</b>
        quickstart that makes it easier to <b>build and scale</b> a web project,
        even when you don’t know the final scope yet?
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-subtitle">
        That's why I created this quickstart project. It’s a thoughtfully
        designed boilerplate project that gives you everything you need to go
        from concept to deployment—with zero guesswork and near-zero overhead.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-subtitle">
        Check out the <a class="text-primary hover:underline" href="https://github.com/cooperjones/astro-cloudflare-kickstart" target="_blank"
                  >Github Repository</a
                > to learn more about the technical stack!
      </p>
      <div class="mt-16">
        <h2>Built to Be Simple by Default, Powerful When Needed</h2>
        <p class="text-description mt-4">
          At its core, this quickstart template is built around Astro, a modern
          static site generator (SSG) that emphasizes zero-JavaScript-by-default
          for blazingly fast performance. Astro is perfect for sites that are
          mostly static but occasionally need sprinkles of interactivity—thanks
          to its Islands Architecture and seamless integration with React and
          other frameworks.
        </p>
        <p class="text-description mt-4">
          By default, your site is entirely static and can be hosted anywhere.
          But with a flip of a switch, you can scale up to dynamic server-side
          rendering, add APIs with Astro Endpoints, and even manage forms or
          backends—all without needing to rethink your architecture. With this
          kickstart project you get:
        </p>
        <ul role="list" class="mt-8 space-y-8 text-muted-foreground">
          <li class="flex gap-x-3">
            <svg
              class="mt-1 size-5 flex-none text-indigo-600"
              viewBox="0 0 20 20"
              fill="currentColor"
              aria-hidden="true"
              data-slot="icon"
            >
              <path
                fill-rule="evenodd"
                d="M5.5 17a4.5 4.5 0 0 1-1.44-8.765 4.5 4.5 0 0 1 8.302-3.046 3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.504 4.272A4 4 0 0 1 15 17H5.5Zm3.75-2.75a.75.75 0 0 0 1.5 0V9.66l1.95 2.1a.75.75 0 1 0 1.1-1.02l-3.25-3.5a.75.75 0 0 0-1.1 0l-3.25 3.5a.75.75 0 1 0 1.1 1.02l1.95-2.1v4.59Z"
                clip-rule="evenodd"></path>
            </svg>
            <span
              ><strong class="font-semibold text-gray-900"
                >SSG by Default.</strong
              > Astro keeps your technical overhead low while making it easy to add
              additional functionality through client side rendering only when you
              need to.
            </span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex gap-x-3">
            <svg
              class="mt-1 size-5 flex-none text-indigo-600"
              viewBox="0 0 20 20"
              fill="currentColor"
              aria-hidden="true"
              data-slot="icon"
            >
              <path
                fill-rule="evenodd"
                d="M10 1a4.5 4.5 0 0 0-4.5 4.5V9H5a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v6a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h10a2 2 0 0 0 2-2v-6a2 2 0 0 0-2-2h-.5V5.5A4.5 4.5 0 0 0 10 1Zm3 8V5.5a3 3 0 1 0-6 0V9h6Z"
                clip-rule="evenodd"></path>
            </svg>
            <span
              ><strong class="font-semibold text-gray-900"
                >Streamlined Dev Experience.</strong
              > At its core, Astro takes care of common web dev chores like image
              optimization, SEO best practices, routing, etc. while keeping development
              simple. Editing .astro files feels like writing plain HTML until you
              want to do something more.</span
            >
          </li>
          <li class="flex gap-x-3">
            <svg
              class="mt-1 size-5 flex-none text-indigo-600"
              viewBox="0 0 20 20"
              fill="currentColor"
              aria-hidden="true"
              data-slot="icon"
            >
              <path
                d="M4.632 3.533A2 2 0 0 1 6.577 2h6.846a2 2 0 0 1 1.945 1.533l1.976 8.234A3.489 3.489 0 0 0 16 11.5H4c-.476 0-.93.095-1.344.267l1.976-8.234Z"
              ></path>
              <path
                fill-rule="evenodd"
                d="M4 13a2 2 0 1 0 0 4h12a2 2 0 1 0 0-4H4Zm11.24 2a.75.75 0 0 1 .75-.75H16a.75.75 0 0 1 .75.75v.01a.75.75 0 0 1-.75.75h-.01a.75.75 0 0 1-.75-.75V15Zm-2.25-.75a.75.75 0 0 0-.75.75v.01c0 .414.336.75.75.75H13a.75.75 0 0 0 .75-.75V15a.75.75 0 0 0-.75-.75h-.01Z"
                clip-rule="evenodd"></path>
            </svg>
            <span
              ><strong class="font-semibold text-gray-900"
                >Efficient and Accessible.</strong
              > Lightning fast. 100/100 Lighthouse performance.</span
            >
          </li>
          <li class="flex gap-x-3">
            <svg
              class="mt-1 size-5 flex-none text-indigo-600"
              viewBox="0 0 20 20"
              fill="currentColor"
              aria-hidden="true"
              data-slot="icon"
            >
              <path
                d="M4.632 3.533A2 2 0 0 1 6.577 2h6.846a2 2 0 0 1 1.945 1.533l1.976 8.234A3.489 3.489 0 0 0 16 11.5H4c-.476 0-.93.095-1.344.267l1.976-8.234Z"
              ></path>
              <path
                fill-rule="evenodd"
                d="M4 13a2 2 0 1 0 0 4h12a2 2 0 1 0 0-4H4Zm11.24 2a.75.75 0 0 1 .75-.75H16a.75.75 0 0 1 .75.75v.01a.75.75 0 0 1-.75.75h-.01a.75.75 0 0 1-.75-.75V15Zm-2.25-.75a.75.75 0 0 0-.75.75v.01c0 .414.336.75.75.75H13a.75.75 0 0 0 .75-.75V15a.75.75 0 0 0-.75-.75h-.01Z"
                clip-rule="evenodd"></path>
            </svg>
            <span
              ><strong class="font-semibold text-gray-900"
                >Fully customizable theme and styles. </strong
              >This template takes advantage of tailwindcss for easy styling and layout customization. Additionally it comes preconfigured with a fully customizable theme and easy component generation to ensure a cohesive design throughout your site. (see <a class="hover:underline text-primary" href="https://ui.shadcn.com/docs">ShadCN documentation</a> for details)</span
            >
          </li>
          <li class="flex gap-x-3">
            <svg
              class="mt-1 size-5 flex-none text-indigo-600"
              viewBox="0 0 20 20"
              fill="currentColor"
              aria-hidden="true"
              data-slot="icon"
            >
              <path
                d="M4.632 3.533A2 2 0 0 1 6.577 2h6.846a2 2 0 0 1 1.945 1.533l1.976 8.234A3.489 3.489 0 0 0 16 11.5H4c-.476 0-.93.095-1.344.267l1.976-8.234Z"
              ></path>
              <path
                fill-rule="evenodd"
                d="M4 13a2 2 0 1 0 0 4h12a2 2 0 1 0 0-4H4Zm11.24 2a.75.75 0 0 1 .75-.75H16a.75.75 0 0 1 .75.75v.01a.75.75 0 0 1-.75.75h-.01a.75.75 0 0 1-.75-.75V15Zm-2.25-.75a.75.75 0 0 0-.75.75v.01c0 .414.336.75.75.75H13a.75.75 0 0 0 .75-.75V15a.75.75 0 0 0-.75-.75h-.01Z"
                clip-rule="evenodd"></path>
            </svg>
            <span
              ><strong class="font-semibold text-gray-900">Extensible.</strong> Use
              the Starlight integration to create a beautiful documentation site.
              Use Astro's server actions to connect to a DB or data source. Use Astro's
              content collections to create a static blog or portfolio without the
              need for a CMS. The possibilities are endless.</span
            >
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <!--<div class="mt-8">
              <h2>One Vendor to Rule Them All</h2>
              <p class="text-description mt-4">
                Managing a modern web app often means piecing together services from a variety of vendors—one for domains, another for DNS, a third for SSL, a fourth for hosting, not to mention separate tools for databases, CAPTCHA, and analytics. Stitching them together can quickly lead to a fragile web of accounts, invoices, and configuration overhead.
              </p>
              <p class="text-description mt-4">
                That complexity comes at a cost—not just financially, but cognitively. Every new vendor introduces more documentation to read, more integration to debug, and more opportunities for things to break during deployment.
              </p>
              <p class="text-description mt-4">
                That’s why this quickstart is built around Cloudflare. With a single account, you get:
              </p>
            </div>-->

      <div
        class="mx-auto mt-16 grid max-w-2xl grid-cols-1 gap-x-8 gap-y-16 lg:mx-0 lg:mt-16 lg:max-w-none lg:grid-cols-12"
      >
        <div class="relative lg:order-last lg:col-span-5">
          <figure class="border-l border-indigo-600 pl-8">
            <blockquote
              class="text-xl/8 font-semibold tracking-tight text-foreground"
            >
              <p>
                “Perfection is achieved, not when there is nothing more to add,
                but when there is nothing left to take away.”
              </p>
            </blockquote>
            <div class="text-sm/6">
              <div class="font-semibold text-foreground">
                - Antoine de Saint-Exupéry
              </div>
            </div>
          </figure>
        </div>
        <div class="max-w-xl text-base/7 lg:col-span-7">
          <h2>One Vendor to Rule Them All</h2>
          <p class="text-description mt-4">
            Here’s where the template really shines: <b>Cloudflare</b>. Instead
            of stitching together multiple providers for domain registration,
            DNS, SSL, hosting, CAPTCHA, and database services, Cloudflare gives
            you a unified platform for all of these services along with a
            generous free hosting tier.
          </p>
          <p class="text-description mt-4">
            With Cloudflare you can get your entire site up and running for <b
              >only the cost of your domain!</b
            >
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="mt-16">
        <h2>Why Use This Kickstart</h2>
        <p class="text-description mt-4">
          At the end of the day, what you are building is more important than
          the tools you use to build it. This kickstart project is designed to
          eliminate friction and accelerate your web development workflow.
          Whether you're building a landing page, a documentation hub, or a
          full-fledged web app, this boilerplate gives you a solid,
          production-ready foundation—without the usual complexity. It combines
          the simplicity of Astro with a thoughtfully curated tech stack and
          first-class integration with Cloudflare, so you can go from idea to
          deployment in minutes. No more wrestling with scattered tools or
          architecture decisions. Just clean code, smart defaults, and the
          flexibility to scale when you're ready.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
      <div class="mt-16 bg-primary py-16">
        <div class="page-section text-primary-foreground">
          <h2 class="mb-4">Ready to get Started?</h2>
          <Button size="lg" as="a" href="https://github.com/cooperjones/astro-cloudflare-kickstart" variant="secondary" target="_blank"
                  >Head over to the Github repository <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></Button
                >
        </div>
      </div>
  </div>
</RootLayout>
